      "product_type": "upper_limit",
      "description": "Observed and expected 95% CL limits on the nonresonant HH production cross section as a function of the Higgs self‑coupling modifier κλ, including ±1σ and ±2σ bands",
      "evidence_span": "Observed and expected limits at 95\\% CL on the cross section of nonresonant Higgs boson pair production as a function of the Higgs boson self-coupling modifier $\\kappa_{\\lambda}= \\lambda_{HHH}/\\lambda^{\\textrm{SM}}_{HHH}$. The  expected constraints on \\klambda are obtained with a background hypothesis excluding $pp \\rightarrow HH$ production.  The $\\pm 1\\sigma$ and $\\pm 2\\sigma$  variations about the expected limit due to statistical and systematic uncertainties are also shown. The theory prediction curve represents the scenario where all parameters and couplings are set to their SM values except for  $\\kappa_{\\lambda}$. The uncertainty band of the  theory prediction curve shows the cross-section uncertainty.",
      "passage_id": 14,
      "confidence": 0.94
    },
    {
      "product_type": "other",
      "description": "Table of observed data events and expected HH signal yields for κλ=1 and κλ=10, plus single‑Higgs and continuum background yields in the 120–130 GeV m_yy window",
      "evidence_span": "The number of data events observed in the  $120<\\myy<130~\\GeV$ window,\nthe number of $HH$ signal events expected for $\\klambda=1$ and for $\\klambda=10$,\nand events expected for single Higgs boson production (estimated using MC simulation),\nas well as for continuum background. For the single Higgs boson, \"Rest\" includes the following production modes: VBF, $WH$, $tHq$, and $tHW$.\nThe values are obtained from a fit of the Asimov data set~\\cite{Cowan:2010js} generated under the SM signal-plus-background hypothesis, $\\klambda = 1$. The continuum background component  of the Asimov data set is obtained from the fit of the data sideband.\nThe uncertainties in $HH$ signals and\nsingle Higgs boson background include the systematic uncertainties discussed in Section~\\ref{sec:systematics}.\nThe uncertainty in the continuum background is given by the sum in quadrature of the statistical uncertainty\nfrom the fit to the data and the spurious-signal uncertainty.",
